Subject: Re: Time-removal (multinomPois): prediction units?
Message-ID: <SAWnXmYLJig.B6eRlfky4soJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <SAWnXmYLJig.PdRmj5CNXJ0J@unmarked.groups.google.com>
References: <SAWnXmYLJig.PdRmj5CNXJ0J@unmarked.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/SAWnXmYLJig/m/B6eRlfky4soJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Poisson regression models the expected count in a given sample, so if you want densities you just have to do the conversion based on the area of your sample (e.g., plot size).  If the plot size changes across sampling units you need to include the log of plot size as a covariate for abundance (or as an offset, if that's available in multinomPois).  Then your expected count is the number of individuals in a plot with a unit area of 1.

