> Error in unique(season) : object 'season' not found

Erik, you are telling R to make a data frame with a factor that has levels defined by the unique values in season.  Season needs to be an object, otherwise where is R getting these unique values?  That code was definitely missing a closing parens where Chris had pointed out.  But season needs to be defined as an object, or the levels of the factor "season" in that data frame need to be explicitly defined (e.g., levels = c("sea.1", "sea.2"...)).

